WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.510
Hollywood loves its sequels.

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:07.000
We're constantly bombarded with trailers,
posters, and concept art for franchise films.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.990
But there are quite a few Part-Twos in the
works that have successfully stayed relatively

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.049
under the radar.

00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:16.540
From Biblical epics to nineties nostalgia-fests,
let's take a look at some of the sequels you

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.240
didn't know were being made.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.090
Edge of Tomorrow 2

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:24.650
The Groundhog Day of alien invasion movies,
2014's Edge of Tomorrow is one of the best

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.650
sci-fi films in recent memory.

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:31.320
Starring Tom Cruise and Emily Blunt, this
Doug Liman flick focuses on a cowardly major

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.040
who finds himself reliving the same day over
and over.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:40.160
Unfortunately, that day involves an army of
extraterrestrials dead set on conquering Earth.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.720
While the film earned rave reviews ...

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:45.100
“Have you ever felt this way before?”

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.410
… it was a major financial disappointment,
so it didn't seem like the Edge of Tomorrow

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.040
story would live to see another day.

00:00:54.989 --> 00:00:59.559
But according to original screenwriter Christopher
McQuarrie, Cruise started pitching a sequel

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.090
while filming Mission Impossible: Rogue Nation.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:06.280
Soon, the screenplay took shape and Blunt
and Liman were on-board for part two.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.889
Sadly, Bill Paxton was also set to return
as the mustachioed Master Sergeant, but the

00:01:10.889 --> 00:01:13.850
beloved actor passed away in February 2017.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:20.249
Liman says the film will be a "sequel that's
a prequel," that is "going to revolutionize

00:01:20.249 --> 00:01:21.740
how people make sequels."

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:27.009
Whatever that all means, it sounds like it
won't just be deja vu, all over again.

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:28.729
The Resurrection

00:01:28.729 --> 00:01:32.450
With the success of Hacksaw Ridge, Mel Gibson
is enjoying something of a comeback.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:37.860
And his next big project is a throwback to
his most successful film: 2004's The Passion

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:38.899
of the Christ.

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:43.689
Passion focused on the last hours of Jesus
Christ's life as he endured torture after

00:01:43.689 --> 00:01:45.759
torture before his death on a cross.

00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:51.329
Despite the unusually gory take on the well-known
tale, Passion became the highest-grossing

00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:53.200
R-rated film in U.S. history.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.799
In August 2016, Gibson announced he was working
on a sequel, a "huge undertaking" called The

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:02.939
Resurrection, with Braveheart scribe Randall
Wallace writing the screenplay.

00:02:02.939 --> 00:02:06.950
In November, Gibson went on The Late Show
with Stephen Colbert and took a few questions

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:10.630
about the follow-up that he says is "likely
still three years out."

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.520
“No, no bad guys?”

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.520
“Well, there are.”

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:13.320
“Yeah?”

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:14.720
“They’re in another realm.”

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.160
“Oh.”

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.750
As Colbert notes, the bible does suggest Jesus
spent three days in hell, so it sounds like

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:26.640
Gibson might have the Messiah tangling with
some literal demons.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.600
2020 can't get here fast enough.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.900
The Equalizer 2

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:40.310
In 40 years of acting on the silver screen
Denzel Washington has never starred in a sequel.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:45.260
But that's all about to change, as Washington
is set to revive Robert McCall, the literature-loving

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.790
hit man from 2014's The Equalizer.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:52.560
Officially announced in April 2015, The Equalizer
2 is getting the band back together.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.670
Washington, director Antoine Fuqua, and screenwriter
Richard Wenk are all back in action.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:01.010
So why is Washington finally agreeing to a
sequel?

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:05.210
Producer Todd Black says the Jason Bourne
series inspired Denzel to finally take the

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:06.420
franchise plunge.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.380
And he's not the only one on the project taking
big risks.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:14.590
Black says Fuqua has a new "effect" planned,
which he can't talk about, but it's "frickin'

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.850
so cool you won't believe it."

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.690
Not even a hint, Dr. Evil?

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.950
“Throw me a frickin’ bone here!”

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:24.360
Guess we'll have to wait, but it sounds "frickin'"
amazing.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.880
Look for The Equalizer 2 in 2018.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.380
The Girl in the Spider's Web

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:34.480
David Fincher's 2011 adaptation of the Stieg
Larsson novel The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.980
didn't earn enough to impress studio executives,
so the next book in the series, The Girl Who

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:42.220
Played with Fire, never made it to the screen
in the U.S.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:47.400
However, in November 2015, it was announced
that everybody's favorite hacker Lisbeth Salander

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:52.460
would finally return — only this time, Hollywood
would adapt The Girl in the Spider's Web,

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:56.760
the latest novel in the Millennium series,
written by David Lagercrantz after Larsson's

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.069
untimely death.

00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:02.710
A year later, it was revealed that Spider's
Web will be helmed by Fede Alvarez, the director

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:06.540
behind Don't Breathe and the 2013 Evil Dead
reboot.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:11.250
The studio also plans on recasting the lead
role, and rumor has it the producers are considering

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.959
Natalie Portman and Scarlett Johansson, among
others.

00:04:13.959 --> 00:04:17.630
Spider's Web is scheduled to hit theaters
October 2018.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.329
The Rocketeers

00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:25.080
Released in 1991 between Robin Hood: Prince
of Thieves and Terminator 2: Judgment Day,

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:30.050
the two highest-grossing movies of the year,
The Rocketeer crashed and burned at the box

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.050
office.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:32.050
killing Disney's hope of establishing an Indiana
Jones-style franchise.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:34.580
But over the years, this World War II-era
adventure has picked up something of a cult

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:39.270
following, inspiring the studio to finally
revisit The Rocketeer universe.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:44.539
In July 2016, Disney finally announced The
Rocketeers, a follow-up taking place about

00:04:44.539 --> 00:04:47.240
six years after the events of the original
film.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:51.860
Our new Rocketeer — yet to be cast — is
an African-American female pilot who finds

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:56.259
herself in the middle of some serious Cold
War intrigue with an evil rocket scientist

00:04:56.259 --> 00:04:59.229
trying to get his hands on the all-powerful
jetpack.

00:04:59.229 --> 00:05:03.930
Interestingly, the film is being co-produced
by NBA star Blake Griffin, who must have a

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:07.360
thing for rocket packs, considering he sported
one in that Gamefly spot …

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.729
“Do you guys have a bathroom?

00:05:09.729 --> 00:05:11.680
Thank you!”

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.430
Hopefully he'll have a cameo.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:14.430
Thanks for watching!

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.099
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:17.099 --> 00:05:19.719
Plus check out all this other cool stuff we
know you'll love, too!

